{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":376907,"duration_api_ms":78682,"ttft_ms":1847,"ttft_stream_ms":1323,"time_to_request_ms":214,"num_turns":21,"result":"## Summary\n\nRoot cause: `DefaultTabDataStore.removeWindowData(forUUIDs:)` in `BrowserKit/Sources/TabDataStore/TabDataStore.swift` only walked the primary `window-data` directory and deleted matching files there — it never touched `window-data-backup`, so backup copies of removed windows accumulated forever.\n\nFix: for each UUID being removed, also compute its backup file path via the existing `windowURLPath(for:isBackup:)` helper and delete it with `fileManager.removeFileAt(path:)`. That method already swallows \"file not found\" errors (just logs at debug level), so windows without a backup file are removed cleanly with no error, and untouched UUIDs (and their backups) are left alone since the loop only acts on UUIDs present in the input list.\n\nAdded 3 tests in `TabDataStoreTests.swift` (plus a `removedPaths` tracker in `MockTabFileManager`) covering: primary+backup both removed for a matching UUID, non-matching UUIDs left untouched in both directories, and the no-directory-found early return. Verified via `xcodebuild test -scheme TabDataStore` — all 23 tests pass.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"79d33e80-3b9b-462d-8545-019339d137f3","total_cost_usd":0.8170248000000002,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":65405,"cache_read_input_tokens":1042406,"output_tokens":7450,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":65405,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":41,"outputTokens":7450,"cacheReadInputTokens":1042406,"cacheCreationInputTokens":65405,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.8170248000000002,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens"